      "writtenOn": "2023-06-27T21:35:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This approach to logging the state was used in the original BT code, however we might reconsider that. My logic when thinking about state logging is as follows. In a function which depends on the state we must have retrieve the state with proper synchronization, this state can be logged. In a function which does not depend on the state logging the state might be unnecessary. Thus usefulness of this sync-free state retrieval needs to be seriously considered, especially that now we have to introduce a thread-safe state getter, making things more confusing.",
      "parentUuid": "ef30ed36_05f9a06c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 188,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "baa1b4190ebbfa0096138ea8f658b6eeb8663050",
