      "writtenOn": "2023-06-27T21:35:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The approach is OK in general, I would suggest several corrections to it:\n\n1. The method needs to be declared on `StreamCommonInterface` as after aosp/2639437 the DriverInterface only contains methods called on the worker thread, while this one is called on the Binder pool thread. It will also be returning `ScopedAStatus` for the same reason.\n\n2. To avoid depending on the particular BT interfaces implementation, I would suggest using AIDL interfaces: `IBluetooth` etc, not node classes (`Bn...`). The interfaces support both setting and retrieving the state thus they should be sufficient.\n\n3. Since the Module implementation anyway keeps strong pointers to BT interface implementations, and they are not supposed to change over Module\u0027s lifetime, we can create them prior creating the first stream, and then pass as parameters to the stream\u0027s constructor. Since now creation of a stream is a virtual function that can be overridden by the Module implementation, it is possible to add any extra parameters. Using a `weak_ptr` is indeed recommended to avoid creating circular references.\n\n4. I would suggest renaming the method to `bluetoothParametersUpdated`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 179,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "baa1b4190ebbfa0096138ea8f658b6eeb8663050",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
